From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roshan Gautam <roshangautam07@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:04:43 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 57/74] deps: update c-ares to 1.34.9

Sync deps/cares with the c-ares 1.34.9 tree shipped by the v20.x and
v22.x security releases. Node.js 18 was on c-ares 1.29.0; c-ares 1.34.9
is a security release fixing, among others, acceptance of DNS replies
from a server other than the one queried, query-cache answers obtained
with different EDNS options, and several use-after-free issues.

The v20.x line made the same 1.29 -> 1.34 move without changes outside
deps/cares other than the test-dns.js expectation adjusted for c-ares
1.31.0, which is included here.

Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases
Refs: a538a9515d (deps: update c-ares to 1.34.9)
Refs: c5174f5e60 (deps: update c-ares to v1.31.0)
