-.B ares_socket_functions
-struct provided is not copied but directly referenced,
-and must thus remain valid through out the channels and any created socket's lifetime.
+These callback functions are invoked while c-ares is part-way through
+creating, connecting, writing to, reading from or closing a socket.  They
+must only perform the requested socket operation and must not call any c-ares
+function on the same channel; for example they must not enqueue or cancel
+queries, process socket events, change the server configuration, or destroy
+the channel.  Doing so is not supported.  Work of that kind belongs in a query
+callback, the server state callback set by
+\fIares_set_server_state_callback(3)\fP, or the socket state callback
+(\fBARES_OPT_SOCK_STATE_CB\fP) described in \fIares_init_options(3)\fP.
+Functions may be called on a different channel.
